35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The car is often returned with the fuel light on and rubbish inside. Also, the mechanic warned that frequent short trips are wearing down the brakes and battery much faster than expected.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"It's a total time sink! Recording every run took nearly an hour a week, and the diary shows we're barely using it on Tuesdays compared to the absolute chaos of Saturdays and holidays.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The fixed costs for tax and insurance are quite substantial, totaling over 280,000 yen. However, I recall that when we tried to scrutinize each other's figures, it only brought tension and apologies. We must be careful not to let numbers erode our harmony.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Other groups said the real problem is having to ask for favors constantly or people hogging turns. Also, our heavy use comes in bursts, which forces us to spend whole evenings just coordinating.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The fuel receipts are all over the place! A couple of us are paying for way more than others, and some barely contribute. Also, those weekly repeat trips are exactly where the scheduling falls apart!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, if the fuel contributions are uneven, that explains why the car is often returned empty. It seems we're neglecting the basic state of the vehicle for the sake of convenience.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Takumi, you hit the nail on the head! Coordinating those bursts of use is a nightmare. Between the scheduling and the recording, we're spending way too much of our free time just managing the car.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is natural for friction to arise when we prioritize convenience over clarity. If we focus only on the imbalance of fuel, we may miss the larger picture of our shared responsibility. How can we balance fairness with peace?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, we can't have peace if we're just pretending everything is fine. If we keep asking for favors or fighting over bursts of use, we're just moving the problem around. We need a system that stops the resentment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I agree that harmony is important, but it's hard to be happy when some of us are paying for everyone else's gas! We need a real system so nobody feels cheated.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"It's not just about the money. If the car isn't ready to drive on a weekday morning because it's dirty or empty, the whole system fails regardless of who paid for the fuel.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,Exactly! It's the mental load that's killing me. We're spending entire evenings just untangling who owes what and when. Is the car even worth it if we spend all our free time managing it?,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Life is too short to spend our precious evenings in conflict over a machine. Perhaps we should seek a solution that simplifies the burden, allowing us to return to the joy of companionship rather than the stress of accounting.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@May, if the mental load is that bad, we can't just ""simplify"" it. We have to fix the root cause. If we don't stop the favor-asking and the hogging, we'll just be stressed in a different way.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, you're right! We can't just ignore the root cause. If we fix the fuel payments and the weekly schedule clashes, the mental load and the fighting will probably go away on their own!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I disagree. Fixing the payments doesn't fix the physical state of the car. We need a rule that ensures the vehicle is clean and fueled for the next person, or the schedule is meaningless.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I agree, but rules only work if they don't take another hour to enforce! If we just add more ""checks,"" we're just adding to the mountain of admin we're already drowning in.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,"True, the weight of administration can stifle the spirit. Let us remember that a rule is merely a tool; if the tool becomes a burden, it no longer serves us. We must find a path of effortless balance.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"Effortless balance is a dream. We need a system that's actually solid. If we don't address the resentment from favors and hogging now, no amount of ""spirit"" will save this group from falling apart.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I think we can do both! If we set up a simple, fair way to split the costs and a fixed schedule for those weekly trips, it'll be way easier to keep the car clean too!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A seems the most stable. If we have fixed days, the person responsible for the car on that day is clearly accountable for its cleanliness and fuel level before the next person takes over.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A sounds like a dream for my schedule! No more endless coordinating or spending my evenings playing accountant. We just know whose turn it is, and that's it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option A offers a serene simplicity that could restore our peace. By accepting a fixed share, we move away from the tension of counting every yen and instead embrace a spirit of mutual trust.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option A is too rigid. If someone has a burst of use or an emergency, we're right back to asking for favors and feeling resentful when someone hogs their day. It doesn't solve the root cause.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I see Takumi's point, but Option A is so much better than guesswork! If we have a fixed monthly share, we finally know exactly what the car costs us every year without any fighting.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Takumi, rigidity is better than uncertainty. If we have a fixed day, I can actually rely on the car being there and ready for me on a Tuesday morning without wondering who left it empty.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Takumi, you're always worrying about the ""what ifs""! I'd rather deal with an occasional favor than spend every single week drowning in spreadsheets and scheduling drama. Let's just pick the easiest path!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, while rigidity may seem cold, there is a certain freedom in knowing exactly where one stands. If we stop measuring every single mile, we may find that the generosity of spirit returns to our group.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, generosity doesn't just happen because we stop counting. If I'm stuck with a day I don't need while someone else is struggling with a house move, the resentment just builds up in silence. That's how groups actually sour.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, but if we use Option C, we'd be back to recording every single mile and spending hours on spreadsheets! That's exactly what May hates. Option A is a fair compromise that gives us a real budget.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"Option C is a nightmare for the car's condition. If we only pay for the distance we drive, nobody will feel responsible for the general upkeep or the battery health the mechanic mentioned.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, exactly! Option C is just a fancy way of saying ""let's spend more time on admin."" I'm not signing up for another year of calculating cents and minutes. Option A is the only one that gives me my evenings back!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is true that Option C invites the very scrutiny that once brought us tension. When we treat a shared bond like a business transaction, we risk losing the warmth of our friendship to the coldness of a ledger.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, the ""warmth"" is already gone because we're all annoyed! Option B is the only one that actually stops the favor-asking cycle. One person is the boss of the car, and we just pay them. No more guessing or fighting.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, but Option B just puts all the stress on one person! That's not fair. Option A is the best because it's simple, it gives us a clear budget, and it stops the guesswork for everyone!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is too risky. If the primary keeper is absent-minded or neglects the car, we're back to square one with a dirty, empty vehicle. Option A ensures a rotating sense of ownership and accountability. I vote for A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"I'm with Misaki! I can't handle any more ""coordinating"" or ""calculating."" Option A is the only one that lets me stop being the group's unpaid accountant. I'm voting for A!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,I believe that a shared life is most beautiful when it is not a series of debts and credits. Option A allows us to move past the ledger and return to a state of grace. I vote for A.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not voting for A. It's just a band-aid that ignores how we actually fight. If we want to stop the resentment and the favor-asking, we need a real change. I'm voting for B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm voting for A too! It's the only way to get a real picture of the costs and stop the guesswork. It's simple, fair, and it lets us be friends again instead of fighting over gas!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
